WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.650
Loops can be combined together with each other

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.800
and with functions to make code both readable and versatile.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.230
In this case, we will show a nested For loop.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.000
A nested For loop is a loop inside another loop.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.490
When we hit the first For statement, we define

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:20.290
the value iX as equal to the first value of the array in the loop declaration.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.610
In this case, the array is an array of doubles.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:25.790
And the value of the first element of the array is 1.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.890
When we hit the second For statement, we define the second variable.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.650
In this case, the variable is iY.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.140
iY will be set equal to the first value of the array

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.870
in this loop&amp;#39;s declaration.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.270
In this case, the array is an array of cells.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.670
iY is, therefore, a cell.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:45.020
The first time through the loop, the cell has the array of characters, LEGO.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.850
Now the code calls for a function that takes two variables and does something.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.537
Our function juggles one LEGO brick.

00:00:51.537 --> 00:00:53.370
Note that, in this case, the function is not

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.680
returning any values when it&amp;#39;s done.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.450
When we hit the first End statement, we repeat the innermost For loop.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.720
The value of iX has not changed.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.770
Only the value of iY has changed.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:07.960
In this case, the second value in our array is a cell with the word &amp;quot;apple.&amp;quot;

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.580
Again, the loop passes the values over to the function.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.466
And the function juggles one apple.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.810
When the end is hit this time, there are no more values in iY array.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.570
Now live proceeds to the next line of code, which is another End

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:26.560
statement, this time for the outermost loop.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.670
Now we increment the value in iX to the second element

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.034
of the array, the value 3.

00:01:32.034 --> 00:01:34.200
The next line of code is a declaration for the inner

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.880
For loop, which we will now run again.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.980
The fact that we ran this before has no influence on how the loop will run now.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.710
The first time we go through the loop, iY

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.195
will still become a cell with the word LEGO.

00:01:46.195 --> 00:01:48.540
The loop passes its values to function.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.100
The function juggles three LEGOs.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.440
The second time the loop runs, the function juggles three apples.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.328
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.400
Now we hit our End statement.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.970
And the code updates the iX value.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.919
There is only one more element in the array,

00:02:09.919 --> 00:02:13.360
so this is the last time we will execute the outermost loop.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.250
This time, the value is set to 84. iX will have a value of 84,

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.030
and iY will have the value LEGO.

00:02:23.202 --> 00:02:26.160
As always, it&amp;#39;s not a bad idea to have your function check to make sure

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.451
that the values are reasonable.

00:02:27.451 --> 00:02:29.580
[MUSIC PLAYING]

